- @root: Return

@diplomacy
title: Diplomacy
subtitle: Improves our standing abroad, and with the minor parties at home.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; europe_relation += 6; us_relation += 6; lib_relation += 4; uup_relation += 3; right_dissent += 2

Carrington charms the diplomats of three continents, and David Steel over lunch.

@lords
title: Steady the grandees
subtitle: Calms the party managers and the rebels.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; loyalist_dissent -= 6; wet_dissent -= 3; rebellion -= 2 if con_in_government

A word in the right ears at White's and the Carlton. The grandees agree to give you the benefit of the doubt.

@mediate
title: Mediate in Cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: Cabinet tension and wet dissent fall.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; cabinet_revolt -= 2; wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 2

Carrington takes the leading wets aside, one by one, and tells them that resigning would only help Labour. He tells you, separately, to let them win an argument now and then.
